# The overhand knot, spelled by its crossings: walking along the rope, under
# crossing 1, over 2, under 3, then over 1, under 2, over 3.
knot overhand
fr "Nœud simple"
en "Overhand knot"
family stopper
abok 514
gauss U1 O2 U3 O1 U2 O3
# The code is the same for both hands: this one closes into the right trefoil.
closure 3_1

expect crossings 3
expect jones 3_1
expect jones "t + t^3 - t^4"
expect clearance >= 1
expect slips untied 3
